  reason: "PURPOSE: serves the v2 self-host census and import-deletion program under gunbc.v1_maintenance_standing.v1_seed_standing. The bridge carries the existing parser acquisition into std.import.ParsedImportObservation, with the consumer token instantiated as v2.std.compilers.lexing.Token. Its class preserves the seed TokenShape constructor identity through the exhaustive acquired_source_tokens_value match, not Rust Debug formatting or v1.compiler.parse.shape_display_name diagnostic labels; constructor changes must stop the seed build. Its lexeme is sliced from the acquired NewlineIndex.char_codes at the acquired span, and import extents remain owned by v1.compiler.parse.parse_import_statement_extents. The former re-tokenization in v1.gunbc.parsed_import_statements is deleted. The source denominator is the same floor_source_inventory projection of the same source ingress used by required-floor preparation, before closure selection or witness policy; no filesystem roster or lexical scanner is added. Consumers classify sources and cause identities in .dag. The host declarations listed here only carry the existing values across the seed boundary. REGISTRY DISPOSITION: free_call.floor_discovery_source_inventory adds an InterpreterPrimitiveDispatchArm plus registry, signature, and dispatch entries; this is NewEscapeHatchOrAdmissionRow under gunbc.v1_maintenance_standing, not cleared by PURPOSE or generated lookup tables. OPERATOR EXCEPTION: 2026-09-13, relayed by fierce-lark in msg_ad65bd2c-8fc7-47e5-87f2-a7310b82aadd (operator: \"yeah you can add the interpreter thing\"). This admits exactly one new InterpreterPrimitiveDispatchArm, free_call.floor_discovery_source_inventory, and its registry/signature/dispatch rows in std.primitives, v1.compiler.infer_method, and the interpreter. No second arm or later signature widening is admitted without a new exception. The arm is deletion debt from landing: delete it with the interpreter, never migrate it. EXPORT DISPOSITION: floor_discovery_source_inventory is crate-visible only; the private floor_source_inventory extraction is shared with existing preparation. No new public seed export is retained.",
  owning_dissolution_lane: "namespace-structural-observations" as RoadmapNodeId,
  trigger: "Delete free_call.floor_discovery_source_inventory and its registry/signature/dispatch rows in the same change that rewires the census to the native route's own context fold exposing the floor's acquired source inventory to dag consumers (perf item C data path). The arm is never migrated. The same native context-fold capability carries parser-produced import members to dag consumers and replaces the bounded import-token projection; extending the frozen v1 parse carrier is not admitted by this exception. Delete the remaining import/token transports when an executing dag consumer can obtain the floor source ingress and its already-acquired lexical stream and parser-delimited import statements directly from the compiler that owns them, without a seed bridge. Reaching the parser symbol without carrying the first acquisition does not satisfy this trigger.",
  current_boundary: "v1_interpreter free_call.parsed_import_statements and free_call.floor_discovery_source_inventory; gunbc.parsed_import_statement_production; v2.workflow.floor_discovery_producer.floor_discovery_source_inventory_live; v1_compiler.cli_run.floor_source_inventory"
